    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Baseline Replication: Difference-in-Differences\"\nformat: html\nexecute:\n  warning: false\n  message: false\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nIn this section, we replicate the core Intent-to-Treat (ITT) econometric models from the evaluation of the Mi Abogado program. The primary outcome of interest is the number of days a child spends living with their biological or adoptive family in a given quarter.\n\nWe estimate two models:\n1. **A Pooled Difference-in-Differences (DiD) Model:** To capture the average treatment effect across the entire post-randomization period.\n2. **An Event Study Model:** To map the dynamic treatment effects quarter-by-quarter and verify the parallel trends assumption in the pre-treatment periods.\n\n## 1. Environment Setup\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(tidyverse)\nlibrary(fixest)       \nlibrary(modelsummary) \nlibrary(broom)        \nlibrary(plotly)       \n\n# Load the synthetic panel data generated in Chapter 1\npanel_data <- read_rds(\"data/synthetic_mi_abogado_panel.rds\")\n```\n:::\n\n\n## 2. Pooled Difference-in-Differences\n\nWe estimate the pooled ITT model where the outcome Y is regressed on strata covariates X, a treatment indicator T, a post-period indicator Post, and their interaction (T * Post). \n\nThe coefficient on the interaction term represents the average difference between the treatment and control groups in the post-period relative to the pre-period. Standard errors are clustered at the child level to account for repeated observations.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# Run the pooled DiD using feols()\ndid_model <- feols(\n  days_with_family ~ treated * post + female + age_group + region,\n  data = panel_data,\n  cluster = ~child_id # Clustering at the level of randomization\n)\n\n# Display a clean table\nmodelsummary(\n  list(\"Days Living with Family\" = did_model),\n  stars = TRUE,\n  gof_omit = \"IC|Log|Adj|Within\",\n  coef_rename = c(\"treated\" = \"Assigned to Mi Abogado (T)\",\n                  \"post\" = \"Post-Randomization\",\n                  \"treated:post\" = \"Treatment x Post (ATE)\")\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<!-- preamble start -->\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.js\"></script>\n\n    <script>\n      // Create table-specific functions using external factory\n      const tableFns_42rh2nychshpo8sinuoz = TinyTable.createTableFunctions(\"tinytable_42rh2nychshpo8sinuoz\");\n      // tinytable span after\n      window.addEventListener('load', function () {\n          var cellsToStyle = [\n            // tinytable style arrays after\n          { positions: [ { i: '22', j: 2 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_av1asswpoz41699u1wm1',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '18', j: 2 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_be2o72sc0ne5e1rebzqy',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '1', j: 2 }, { i: '2', j: 2 }, { i: '3', j: 2 }, { i: '4', j: 2 }, { i: '5', j: 2 }, { i: '6', j: 2 }, { i: '7', j: 2 }, { i: '8', j: 2 }, { i: '9', j: 2 }, { i: '10', j: 2 }, { i: '11', j: 2 }, { i: '12', j: 2 }, { i: '13', j: 2 }, { i: '14', j: 2 }, { i: '15', j: 2 }, { i: '16', j: 2 }, { i: '17', j: 2 }, { i: '19', j: 2 }, { i: '20', j: 2 }, { i: '21', j: 2 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_dz5vrov09nz6zdjejlh7',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '0', j: 2 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_3ti82qtyw5tv2wsnse0v',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '22', j: 1 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_agowdk9xhtcnzr0by87a',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '18', j: 1 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_sh34iqx7eqvb29eztial',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '1', j: 1 }, { i: '2', j: 1 }, { i: '3', j: 1 }, { i: '4', j: 1 }, { i: '5', j: 1 }, { i: '6', j: 1 }, { i: '7', j: 1 }, { i: '8', j: 1 }, { i: '9', j: 1 }, { i: '10', j: 1 }, { i: '11', j: 1 }, { i: '12', j: 1 }, { i: '13', j: 1 }, { i: '14', j: 1 }, { i: '15', j: 1 }, { i: '16', j: 1 }, { i: '17', j: 1 }, { i: '19', j: 1 }, { i: '20', j: 1 }, { i: '21', j: 1 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_aqy0matnvnqmla5ny46g',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '0', j: 1 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_yxyf5sfxhc2mnln7ugek',}, \n          ];\n\n          // Loop over the arrays to style the cells\n          cellsToStyle.forEach(function (group) {\n              group.positions.forEach(function (cell) {\n                  tableFns_42rh2nychshpo8sinuoz.styleCell(cell.i, cell.j, group.css_id);\n              });\n          });\n      });\n    </script>\n\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.css\">\n    <style>\n    /* tinytable css entries after */\n    #tinytable_42rh2nychshpo8sinuoz td.tinytable_css_av1asswpoz41699u1wm1, #tinytable_42rh2nychshpo8sinuoz th.tinytable_css_av1asswpoz41699u1wm1 {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 0; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.1em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.1em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%; ; text-align: center }\n    #tinytable_42rh2nychshpo8sinuoz td.tinytable_css_be2o72sc0ne5e1rebzqy, #tinytable_42rh2nychshpo8sinuoz th.tinytable_css_be2o72sc0ne5e1rebzqy {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 0; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.05em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.1em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bot